  "id": "Compound::DB00241 - Gene::2556",
  "verbalization": "Butalbital exhibits a consistent interaction with Gabra3 through a series of molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that Butalbital binds to Gabra6, a subunit of the GABA A receptor, which is a key component of the GABAergic system. This binding leads to the participation of Gabra6 in GABA A receptor activation, and ultimately, Gabra3 is involved in this process. The overlapping pathways across the three paths—binding to Gabra6, participation in receptor activation, and involvement in Gabra3—provide a coherent mechanism for the observed relationship.\n\nThe integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Butalbital in modulating GABA A receptor function, possibly through interactions with Gabra6. The scores from the paths indicate a strong, albeit slightly varying, level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that Butalbital may influence GABA A receptor activity via Gabra6 and, consequently, Gabra3. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this mechanism supports the hypothesis that Butalbital interacts with Gabra3 through a GABA A receptor-mediated pathway.",
